{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/885466-sidereals-wfhl-melee-the-spear","id":885466,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Melee : The Spear","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-08T10:16:03-07:00","id":885466,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Melee : The Spear","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">MELEE : THE SPEAR</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">THE SCRIPTURE OF THE MAIDEN ON THE SHELF</span></span></b><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Once, there was a maiden\u2026</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u2026who sat on a child\u2019s shelf and watched the entire world.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Her eyes were made of glass,</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>And their pupils were red.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Her mouth was sewn on.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>For years and years, she did not move.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Then, when necessary, she was gone, and the head of that child with her.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u201cSurvival is control,\u201d she said.</i></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Spear is skill and discipline in armed conflict. In the ascending aspect, those under its domain display skill, professionalism and discipline. In the descending aspect, they display superficial professionalism, myopia and the inability to see alternate solutions outside their scope of interest. The Spear is the constellation of the bodyguard, the long-service professional soldier, the skilled militiaman, the arms instructor, the mercenary and other skilled professional competitors such as gamblers, gladiators and athletes.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trappings</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Spear wears a uniform but possesses no rank. He is called by his family name or nickname. He is disciplined and brave.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Correlations</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bravery, professionalism, training, taking initiative, lack of vision, tactics, skillfulness, competition</span></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/c88Sb9F.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Resplendent Destiny of the Spear</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (10m); <b>Mins:</b> Melee 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Create a persona. With an Essence 2 repurchase, the Sidereal more fully embodies the destiny; she may use Profile Character actions to determine how many dots of Dodge, Martial Arts, Melee, or War a character has, and substitute her Melee for her Investigation when doing so.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Battle Carrying Presence</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Spear strikes down the fear that would steal the heart of every soldier in battle. With an invigorating shout, the Sidereal makes a reflexive rally action (Exalted pg. 210)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Shield of Mars</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Spear knows that caution is sometimes the better part of valor, and the Shield of Mars shelters those who fight with care. When she uses this charm, the Sidereal may include a Full Defense action (Exalted pg. 196) in a flurry without the initiative or defense penalty.<br /> If she has a weapon with the 'Shield' tag, then she may also include an attack action in this flurry.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>The Queen of Battle</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Stackable<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The essence of the Spear is control; control of one's self, of the field, and of the enemy. By using The Queen of Battle, the Sidereal takes control of her hand-to-hand weapon, adding one of the following tags; 'Balanced', 'Bashing', 'Chopping', 'Lethal', or 'Reaching'. She may add up to (Essence) tags concurrently, but must activate The Queen of Battle for each tag separately.<br /> At Essence 3, she may also add the following tags; 'Disarming', 'Flexible', 'Piercing' or 'Smashing'.<br /> This effect ends if the Sidereal is disarmed or voluntarily lays her weapon down.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>No Retreat</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> There is no retreat from the Spear, save as the Spear allows. When an opponent attempts to disengage from the Sidereal, she may activate No Retreat. Subtract a number of successes equal to his current onslaught penalty. If she is in the Destiny of the Spear, she also increases her opponent's target number to Disengage by 1.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Fighting in the Shade</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> There is no escape from the Spear, save as the Spear allows. When the Sidereal is targeted by a ranged attack before her action, she may use Fighting in the Shade, and counting the number of 1s rolled on the attack to any Rush action she takes towards her attacker this turn, adding them as automatic successes non-charm successes on her rush. If she is in the Destiny of the Spear, she counts any 1s and 2s rolled, and increases the target number of any effort to oppose her rush by 1.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Slow Blade Penetrates</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> When one has control, exploit it; when one lacks control, regain it. When the Sidereal enhances a withering hand to hand attack with Slow Blade Penetrates, increase her post-soak damage by (the higher of her or her target's Onslaught penalty). When she enhances a decisive hand to hand attack, add half of (the higher of her or her target's Onslaught penalty) to the damage roll.<br /> With an Essence 2 repurchase, combine the Onslaught penalties instead of taking the highest.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Essence Draining Battle Pattern</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute, Design<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until the battle's end<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Battle Carrying Presence<br /> <br /> The Maiden of Battles knows the Seven Undefeated Stratagems of Victory, methods of organizing troops that ensure victory against any force. In the name of Mars, the Chosen of Destiny may enact one upon Creation. By activating this charm, the Sidereal may select a special stratagem for her Strategic Maneuver roll, 'Essence Draining Battle Pattern' (Threshold 2), in addition to up to one mundane stratagem; she must overcome the combined threshold or gain the benefit of neither stratagem.<br /> While the Essence Draining Battle Pattern is in effect, opponents gain only 3 motes per turn instead of 5, and all Charms used by an enemy cost an additional 1 mote to activate. This effect ends if the battle group under the Sidereal's command suffers dissolution.<br /> Anyone checking the omens before the battle may notice the alignment of Mars and Jupiter that signify this battle pattern is in place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Impeding the Flow</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The Sidereal knows the approach of the arrow before the archer has drawn it; they have followed the fall of the blade before the swordsman has begun the swing. She may parry any attack which may be parried; she cannot parry attacks which are unblockable, which have no physical component, or events of uncountable or recurring damage.<br /> After each use of Impeding the Flow, the cost to use it again in the same scene increases by 1 mote and 1 initiative. So, the second use costs 4 motes and 2 initiative; the third costs 5 motes and 3 initiative, and so on.<br /> Using Impeding the Flow to block a decisive attack costs an additional 1 temporary willpower point.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Orchestration of Conflict</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1i; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Impeding the Flow<br /> <br /> Battles rage like wild fires, and roar like rivers- but to the disciplined mind, all have their patterns, and may be directed by appropriate forces. By using Orchestration of Conflict, the Sidereal may make herself the target of an attack directed at an ally within Close range.<br /> With a repurchase at Essence 3 and by spending an additional 1 temporary willpower point when activating Orchestration of Conflict, the Sidereal may redirect any attack made within Close range of her to anyone else also within Close range.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Demon Blocking Battle Pattern</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute, Design<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until the battle's end<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Battle Carrying Presence<br /> <br /> The Maiden of Battles knows the Four Devil Stratagems, and the precise counter for each- methods of deploying troops to negate the advantages of fell magic wielded by the enemies of the gods. By activating this charm, the Sidereal may select a special stratagem for her Strategic Maneuver roll, 'Demon Blocking Battle Pattern' (Threshold 2), in addition to up to one mundane stratagem; she must overcome the combined threshold or gain the benefit of neither stratagem.<br /> While the Demon Blocking Battle Pattern is in effect, reduce the Might of opposing units composed primarily of demons, undead or creatures of the wyld by 1.<br /> Anyone checking the omens before the battle may notice the alignment of Mars and Saturn that signify this battle pattern is in place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Hero Supporting Performance</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Impeding the Flow<br /> <br /> The Spear leads by example, and those who trust the Sidereal find fate favoring their steps. By spending a temporary willpower point, the Sidereal may use any number of instant duration Melee charms to enhance an ally's attack or defense whom she can see.<br /> At Melee 5, Essence 3, she may use any instant duration charms to enhance an ally's attack or defense; the charm used must be compatible with the action being taken. (For example, she cannot use Slow Blade Penetrates to enhance an ally's archery attack, because Slow Blade Penetrates specifies that it enhances a melee attack)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Edge of the Knife</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> No Retreat or Fighting in the Shade<br /> <br /> Victory is never certain, defeat is never foregone. Always both are balanced on the edge of a knife. An withering hand to hand attack the Sidereal enhances with Edge of the Knife adds 3 raw damage per failure in the attack roll.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Serenity in Blood</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> (1wp, 1lhl); <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Orchestration of Conflict or Hero Supporting Performance<br /> <br /> Every path of every spear thrown, every route of every axe swung, every cry of exhaulting victory, every scream of pain and despair; the Spear knows them all before dawn breaks on the day of battle. The Sidereal partakes of this knowledge, enhancing a use of Impeding the Flow. When enhanced by Serenity in Blood, Impeding the Flow loses the initative cost and the Perilious keyword, and may block attacks which are normally unblockable, which have no physical component, or which consistent of uncountable recurring damage.<br /> The first time Impeding the Flow is enhanced with Serenity in Blood, it costs an additional 1 lethal health level and 1 temporary willpower point; each additional time, the cost rises by 1, so the second use of Serenity in Blood costs 2 lethal health levels and 2 temporary willpower points, the third use costs 3 lethal health levels and 3 temporary willpower points, and so on. This cost is in addition to the normal mote cost of for however many times Impeding the Flow has already been used.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Spirit Binding Battle Pattern</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute, Design<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until the battle's end<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Battle Carrying Presence<br /> <br /> The Maiden of Battles knows the singular Eightfold Drowning Siege of Heaven strategy, by which the Exalted once lured the enemies of the gods into ill-omened battles. By activating this charm, the Sidereal may select a special stratagem for her Strategic Maneuver roll, 'Spirit Binding Battle Pattern' (Threshold 2), in addition to up to one mundane stratagem; she must overcome the combined threshold or gain the benefit of neither stratagem.<br /> With the Spirit Binding Battle Pattern, the Sidereal sanctifies the deaths of the soldiers fighting, transforming them into an irresistible lure and chain for a spirit.<br /> For every point of Magnitude damage inflicted over the course of the battle, she gains 1 'spirit binding' die. For every point of Size lost, she gains 3 dice. When any battle group is broken, and for each turn the Slaughter action is performed, she gains 5 dice. At any point during the battle, she may spend 1 willpower and attempt to call forth a specifically named god, elemental or demon and bind it to some task. She splits her accumulated spirit binding dice between the call and the binding, to any degree she wishes.<br /> The difficulty of calling the spirit is equal to the Essence of the spirit. The difficulty of the binding is equal to the permanent Willpower of the spirit. If the binding is successful, the spirit gains an unbreakable Defining Principle to complete a task the Sidereal specifies for the next year, after which, gods and elementals are free and demons are cast back to Hell.<br /> The Sidereal may call a spirit without attempting to bind it but many, especially among the Gods, take being offense at being summoned in this cavalier a fashion; likewise, she may attempt to bind a spirit which is already present at the scene of the battle without calling first. Spirit Binding Battle Pattern cannot overcome a sorcerous binding upon a demon, nor the bond between a familiar and his master.<br /> Anyone checking the omens before the battle may notice the alignment of Mars and Venus that signify this battle pattern is in place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Harmony of Blows</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Decisive-only, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> No Retreat or Fighting in the Shade<br /> <br /> The Spear is never out-numbered, but she can find herself in unusually target rich environments. When the Sidereal uses Harmony of Blows, she divides her initiative evenly between up to two targets, and makes a decisive attack against each. The attacks may be made with different abilities, as long as both targets are legal and the Sidereal could take a Ready Weapon action to equip an appropriate armament. If the attacks are made with the same ability, any charms which enhance one attack enhance both.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Meditation on War</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Shield of Mars or The Queen of Battle or Slow Blade Penetrates<br /> <br /> The chaos and confusion of battle hide a secret order; by perceiving this order, the Spear may always act in perfect control. Once per scene, when the Sidereal does not like the outcome of an non-extended action they have just taken, they may spend 1 temporary willpower point to undo that action- it was a vision of a possibility she has discarded. She and anyone else who contested the action regain any spent resources, and the Sidereal must take some other meaningfully distinct course of action- she can still attack, but must attack another target in range; she can still rush, but must rush in another direction.<br /> Meditation of War can be reset by winning an Initiative Shift.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Perfection of the Visionary Warrior</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1wp, 1lhl; <b>Mins:</b> Melee 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Prayer Strip<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Meditation of War, Serenity in Blood, either one of Edge of the Knife or Harmony of Blows, any one of Essence Draining Battle Pattern, Demon Blocking Battle Pattern or Spirit Binding Battle Pattern<br /> <br /> The essence of gaining control lives in giving up control; the essence of harmony lives in accepting things as they are rather than imposing a false harmony upon them. With harmony and control, all things becomes possible. The Sidereal binds a prayer strip marked with the Scripture of the Maiden on the Shelf across her eyes and around her head; it flashes ruby red, tightening and squeezing tears of blood from her.<br /> For the remainder of the scene, the Sidereal does not incur onslaught penalties from any source, and ignores all penalties related to vision or her environment upon her attacks and defenses made within close range. Once per turn, she may choose to force a hand to hand attack into being a clash, even if she has already acted this turn.<br /> Perfection of the Visionary Warrior ends if the Sidereal does not either attack or advance towards any enemy with each action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 05-08-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:31:42-07:00","id":888825,"title":"","content":"Demon Blocking Battle Pattern lacks any narrative description of its method of function that makes sense at the personal scale. The Might score is reduced, but Might is an abstraction of concrete capabilities; if I'm fighting a demon in hand to hand combat in a mass battle where the Demon Blocking Battle Pattern, how is that demon disadvantaged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:22:41-07:00","id":888991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/885466-sidereals-wfhl-melee-the-spear?p=888825#post888825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon Blocking Battle Pattern lacks any narrative description of its method of function that makes sense at the personal scale. The Might score is reduced, but Might is an abstraction of concrete capabilities; if I'm fighting a demon in hand to hand combat in a mass battle where the Demon Blocking Battle Pattern, how is that demon disadvantaged?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tricky. The original Demon Blocking Battle Pattern imposed a general penalty (reducing both attack and defense) by potentially staggering amounts- but any particular penalty that can be applied to an individual could also be applied to a battle group.<br /> <br /> I mean- you're not *wrong*, but compare with the troop upgrades in Tiger Warrior Training Technique, Demon-Fighting Principle and Giant-Slaying Tactics. Both cases increase the group's Might against certain types of foes, despite not changing the stats of individual fighters.<br /> <br /> I'll have to give this a ponder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:19:07-07:00","id":889175,"title":"","content":"To my mind, if there is any great vice in the charms of Exalted 3e, it is a tendency for them to be narratively barren - for them to have no real representation or conception beyond the context of game mechanics so abstract that there's no intuitive way to visualize them. Lookin' at you, Craft charms!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:31:52-07:00","id":889186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/885466-sidereals-wfhl-melee-the-spear?p=889175#post889175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, if there is any great vice in the charms of Exalted 3e, it is a tendency for them to be narratively barren - for them to have no real representation or conception beyond the context of game mechanics so abstract that there's no intuitive way to visualize them. Lookin' at you, Craft charms!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, nice way to put that succinctly. To me, the best charms are the ones that start with the narrative conceit, and work from there. You should be able to describe what a charm does easily without mechanical terms or abstractions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:35:48-07:00","id":889190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/885466-sidereals-wfhl-melee-the-spear?p=889175#post889175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To my mind, if there is any great vice in the charms of Exalted 3e, it is a tendency for them to be narratively barren - for them to have no real representation or conception beyond the context of game mechanics so abstract that there's no intuitive way to visualize them. Lookin' at you, Craft charms!</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, a fair point.<br /> <br /> On the other hand... media of MANY types seem to have a &quot;make supernatural beings uncomfortable and less likely to pwn you, but not actively wounded or driven away&quot; debuff. In a world full of dice tricks, calling out &quot;what exactly is garlic doing to vampires&quot; startles me, somewhat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T09:37:06-07:00","id":889191,"title":"","content":"Every time I read the flavor test for <u>Experiential Conjuring of True Void</u> I become cross and my brow furrows and I tear off my legs<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/885466-sidereals-wfhl-melee-the-spear?p=889190#post889190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a world full of dice tricks, calling out &quot;what exactly is garlic doing to vampires&quot; startles me, somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>C'mon, this isn't a hard question to answer! Garlic is unpleasant to vampires. They don't like it and the smell repulses them, driving them away. This is not narratively barren! This is narratively succinct and specific, and easy to model on a character-by-character level!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}